{# gfadmin/templates/admin/form.html rendered with an OrderItemForm
   (givefood/forms.py:213-216) -- `fields = "__all__"` on a three-field model
   whose `slug` is editable=False, so Django renders precisely these two
   inputs, in model-declaration order (givefood/models/orders.py:293-295).

   Its own template rather than admin/generic_form.njk + an AdminFieldSpec
   list, for two reasons:
     1. `calories` is a PositiveIntegerField, and Django's widget for one is
        genuinely <input type="number" min="0"> (IntegerField's default
        NumberInput + PositiveIntegerField.formfield()'s min_value=0).
        AdminFieldKind has no "number" member, and widening that shared union
        for one two-field form is a bigger change than this file.
     2. This form re-renders itself on a validation failure with the values
        the admin typed plus an error banner (see routes/admin/items.ts);
        generic_form.njk has no error slot, and its callers all return a bare
        text/plain 400 instead.
   Django's own admin/form.html:22-32 right-hand preview column (`{% if need %}`
   / `{% if foodbank %}`) never renders for these two screens -- item_form
   sets neither -- so there is nothing to port there.

   id="id_<name>" matches what Django's `{{ form|bulma }}` emits and what
   static/js/admin.js selects on (admin.js:97-111); none of its initialisers
   fire on this form (they are all gated on #id_lat_lng, #id_company or a
   food-bank/location/donation-point form class), which is correct -- Django's
   items form has no lookup buttons either.

   FIXES admin/form.html:8-10's column-is-half bug (defect class named in
   generic_form.njk's own header comment): Bulma's `.column.is-half` is a
   hard 50% whether or not a sibling column exists, and this page NEVER
   gets a second column (the preview never renders here, per the note
   above), so pinning it drew every visit to this form as a permanent
   half-width strip with an empty right half. #}
{% extends "admin/page.njk" %}

{% block title %}{{ title }}{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="columns">
  <div class="column">
    <h1 class="title">{{ title }}</h1>
    <p><a href="/admin/items/">&larr; Back</a></p>

    {# Django's {{ form|bulma }} shows per-field validation errors inline
       (admin/form.html:16). This port validates in the route, so an invalid
       submission comes back as one banner plus the values the admin typed --
       rather than the text/plain 400 the other ported forms return, which
       throws the typed values away. #}
    {% if error %}<div class="notification is-danger is-light">{{ error }}</div>{% endif %}

    {# class="form-<slugified title>" matches Django admin/form.html:14's
       `class="form-{{ page_title|slugify }}"` -- "form-new-item" /
       "form-edit-item". #}
    <form method="post" class="form-{{ title | slugify }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">

      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="id_name">Name *</label>
        <div class="control">
          <input class="input" type="text" id="id_name" name="name" value="{{ data.name }}" maxlength="100" required>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="id_calories">Calories *</label>
        <div class="control">
          <input class="input" type="number" id="id_calories" name="calories" value="{{ data.calories }}" min="0" step="1" required>
        </div>
        {# models/orders.py:295 help_text="Per 100g". #}
        <p class="help">Per 100g</p>
      </div>

      {# admin/form.html:14's `onclick="this.form.submit();this.disabled = true;"`
         double-submit guard, on every Django admin submit button -- this
         one had been dropped. #}
      <div class="field">
        <div class="control">
          <button type="submit" class="button is-link is-light" onclick="this.form.submit();this.disabled = true;">Submit</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </form>

    {# No delete control: gfadmin/urls/items.py declares no delete route, so
       there is nothing to port. #}
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
